{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1016877-2e-bostonian-alchemist","id":1016877,"title":"[2E] Bostonian Alchemist","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-13T19:55:43-08:00","id":1016877,"title":"[2E] Bostonian Alchemist","content":"In my <b>Mage/Promethen </b>game in Boston, I need Alchemist antagonist character. I still have a problem with grasping all of their themes, so maybe you can help me. I probably want from this character to be:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Women ( I\u2019m progressive ST, giving equal time for both male and female antagonists <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )</li> <li>At least surviving from the time of Golden Dawn affair ( for local historical reasons and plots ), circa 1900s.</li> </ol>I probably can just make her \u2018I\u2019m in Alchemy for immortality\u2019 kinda thing, but this feel to it flattens whole Alchemists idea. Was thinking about making her Chinese ( or at least Chinese descendent ), but this could seems a bit ethnic offensive and clash with highlighting some themes of local Golden Dawn thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 12-13-2016, 11:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T00:31:21-08:00","id":1016931,"title":"","content":"Reading more on subject, I think that Alchemist would be in 1900 wealthy women interested in occult and Alchemy, probably lesbian. I'm still thinking what could be her reason to become Insensate Alchemist and her future from them. As 'semi-wealthy women employing her Sleepers help' can make varied antagonist for PCs, will probably go this route. Still, have problem grasping more idea on her motives than 'everlasting beauty'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T13:00:27-08:00","id":1017239,"title":"","content":"Vengeance. 1900 Boston was NOT a great place to be a woman, let alone a lesbian. Her motives/activities could include using the power of Alchemy to get revenge on her oppressors, or their descendants.<br /> <br /> \u200bPower. Living forever is nice; living like you own the place is better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T05:58:28-08:00","id":1017610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1016877-2e-bostonian-alchemist?p=1017239#post1017239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vengeance. 1900 Boston was NOT a great place to be a woman, let alone a lesbian. Her motives/activities could include using the power of Alchemy to get revenge on her oppressors, or their descendants.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you want more grey, she could be in it to make things better for women rather than avenge herself on men - she's into alchemy as a means to live long enough to make that happen. Or maybe she started out that way, but the things she's done to keep living have hardened to the point where her goals are no longer so noble.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T06:42:15-08:00","id":1017622,"title":"","content":"Cool idea <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6138_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6138\" data-vbnamecard=\"6138\">Mangle77</a> and nice twist <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"321\" data-vbnamecard=\"321\">SunlessNick</a>! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Yes, I can totally see her as starting Alchemy to change Victorian patriarchy, only too ending hunting males on vengeance and Created to sustain her mission. Even with <a href=\"http://www.huffingtonpost.com/2013/10/03/top-10-lgbt-employment-states_n_4039423.html\" target=\"_blank\">New England being one of most gay-friendly places in USA</a>, she still thinks women and homosexuals are treated not good enough. In reality, she will probably <i>never</i> forgive men just being in society. Being ethereally young is nice addition. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Also, interesting question on Alchemists - Does killing Promethean is Breaking Point for them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T13:17:50-08:00","id":1017771,"title":"","content":"I have a name for her - Margaret Westcott, American alchemist from 1900s Boston bohema, very far related to <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/William_Wynn_Westcott\" target=\"_blank\">William Wynn Westcott</a>. Margaret, by decades now, faked her own death after next circa 20 years and show herself as her own next 'niece', inheriting fortune of her 'aunt'. Now she is official Evelyn Thompson. Still, do not have idea on the help she can employ as her servants.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-15T19:02:03-08:00","id":1017904,"title":"","content":"If you need a very memorable character, look up Isabella Stewart Gardner. She'd make a good base for the character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>GM of the <i>Walking Shadow</i> Campaigns</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/8992-the-hacks-and-houserules-of-walking-shadows\" target=\"_blank\">New System and Setting Material</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1040-neotiamat","name":"NeoTiamat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1040_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"471"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-24T08:47:27-08:00","id":1021582,"title":"","content":"Reading now <b>Hurt Locker</b>, I think about giving support group to the Margaret / Evelyn. I was thinking about extremist feminism group, made of women hurt by man - physical abuse, rapes, even just mistreating of husbands. They started by literal abuse support group, now they are much more extreme and recruit mostly from Internet, even if still sticking to Boston terrain. Most of the time they just goes to rallies or protests. But they also teach members in self-defense. And once in a few months, they make more than just next occupation of prominent male politic. Margaret/Evelyn sponsor them from her century long wealth, her latest lover is hailing from group. She advise group on attacking of most prominent men in Boston. She only just ask them once or twice a year to kidnap strange beings that are not even humans\u2026<br /> <br /> You think it\u2019s okay, or maybe I\u2019m overdoing it? I still needs a name for this group.<br /> <br /> Here are Violence Group traits\u2026<br /> <br /> <b>Group Name: </b>Women's Embrace<br /> <b>Concept:</b> Extremist support group<br /> <b>Aspirations:</b> Defeat \u2018misogynists\u2019, Help woman in need, Support women equality<br /> <b>Virtue:</b> Support (\u201cFight with man oppression!\u201d)<br /> <b>Vice:</b> Wrath<br /> <b>Average Member: </b>Social 5, Physical 4, Mental 2<br /> <b>Group Merits: </b>Allies ( Women) 3, Contacts ( Activists ), Danger Sense, Fame 1, Organization Size 2, Resources 2, Safe Place 3, Status 2, Street Fighting 3","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrd